But it also much like most really great how I made your mother episodes, has this undercurrent of pathos and reality to it, which is time is passing.
但它也像大多数《老爸老妈浪漫史》的精彩剧集一样，有一种悲伤和现实的潜流，那就是时光流逝。

00:27:27.059 --> 00:27:28.579
Yeah, and who am I now?
是的，现在的我是谁？

00:27:28.579 --> 00:27:29.420
Who am I?
我是谁？

00:27:29.420 --> 00:27:30.700
If I let go of this thing, who am I?
如果我放手这个东西，我是谁？

00:27:30.700 --> 00:27:33.140
Loss is woven into a life.
失去是编织在生活里的。

00:27:33.140 --> 00:27:34.980
Yes, yes, yes.
是的，是的，是的。

00:27:34.980 --> 00:27:52.940
And when you relinquish a kind of object or memento, much like stuff in a way, that was less the pillow from the girlfriend or whatever, but objects take on a kind of frequency or resonance when we have them for a while.
当你放弃某种物品或纪念品时，就像某种东西一样，虽然它不像女朋友留下的枕头之类的，但当我们拥有它们一段时间后，物体会带有一种频率或共鸣。

00:27:52.940 --> 00:28:04.019
Yeah, it was good to begin this episode with that idea of like the little things we cling to, the guy with the tattoo and the woman with the like little, you know, the piercing, like there's those things you hold on and you think, well, this is me.
是的，以这种我们紧抓不放的小事作为开端很好，那个有纹身的男人，还有那个有小穿孔的女人，你知道，有些东西你紧紧抓住，觉得“嗯，这就是我”。

00:28:04.019 --> 00:28:05.180
This grounds me as me.
这让我感到脚踏实地。

00:28:05.180 --> 00:28:10.779
And when you let go of those things, whether it's letting go of a childhood home or a pet dyes or like, these are rights of passage.
当你放手这些东西时，无论是离开童年的家还是宠物去世，这些都是成长的仪式。

00:28:10.779 --> 00:28:17.579
It's not as huge as like a person in your life dying, but it's like there's all these little funerals, right?
它不像你生命中重要的人去世那么巨大，但就像是有很多小小的葬礼，对吧？

00:28:17.579 --> 00:28:20.940
There are those little memorializations that we have along the way.
我们一路上都有那些小小的纪念仪式。

00:28:20.940 --> 00:28:22.140
And this is one of them.
而这就是其中之一。

00:28:22.140 --> 00:28:30.180
This is, yeah, and it's attached to the object is a kind of like stand-in or representative for the person we were.
这是，是的，它附着在物体上，就像是我们曾经那个人的替身或代表。

00:28:30.180 --> 00:28:32.039
And the person we no longer are.
以及我们不再是的那个人。

00:28:33.500 --> 00:28:38.539
My older sister Melanie helped me move out of my house in L.A., which I sold this past summer.
我姐姐梅兰妮帮我搬出了我在洛杉矶的房子，我去年夏天把它卖了。

